WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:03.951
You put the leaver in order: block first,

3
00:00:03.951 --> 00:00:07.700
revoke in parallel,
reconcile, and dispose last.

4
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.659
You defined separation-to-block
and separation-to-revocation,

5
00:00:11.659 --> 00:00:13.562
and the records each one reads.

6
00:00:13.562 --> 00:00:18.086
You measured fictional leavers and
found the ones that were blocked late,

7
00:00:18.086 --> 00:00:21.349
never blocked, re-enabled,
failed, or deleted too early.

8
00:00:21.349 --> 00:00:25.363
And you saw why the tenant schedule
belongs inside the approved interval.

9
00:00:25.363 --> 00:00:31.650
Next is Module 7, the last in the path:
find lifecycle drift and file the evidence.

10
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:36.252
It writes one read-only run of
six drift classes and six metrics,

11
00:00:36.252 --> 00:00:39.615
reads this module's
percentiles as two of them,

12
00:00:39.615 --> 00:00:43.820
and packages each run with a
hash chain an ISSO can verify.
